  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Product Development Partnerships Funds (PDP III and PDP IV)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Product Development Partnerships Funds (PDP III and PDP IV) contribute to innovation in the areas of healthcare products and technologies specifically aimed at diseases and conditions related to poverty and sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR).The Product Development Partnerships Funds (PDP III and PDP IV) are executed by the Netherlands Enterprise Agency, on behalf of the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs. The PDPs in these programmes, and in that of its predecessor, PDP II, are part of the EDCTP2 Programme, supported by the European Union.Url = http://www.edctp.org/Factsheet: Product Development Partnerships Funds (PDP III)Url = https://projects.rvo.nl/sites/default/files/rvo_website_content/opendata/iati/PDP/PDP-III_01.pdfFor more information: Product Development Partnerships IV Fund (on english.rvo.nl)Url = https://english.rvo.nl/subsidies-financing/pdp-iv</narrative>
  </description>
